---
const services = [
  { name: 'Next.js console', detail: 'shadcn/ui · TanStack Query', kind: 'ui' },
  { name: 'FastAPI', detail: '/api/v1 · JWT + RBAC · rate limits', kind: 'core' },
  { name: 'Celery worker + beat', detail: 'evidence · re-checks · cache', kind: 'core' },
  { name: 'Open Policy Agent', detail: 'Rego policy packs', kind: 'dep' },
  { name: 'PostgreSQL 16', detail: 'append-only audit via triggers', kind: 'dep' },
  { name: 'Redis 7', detail: 'broker · cache · rate-limit store', kind: 'dep' },
  { name: 'S3-compatible storage', detail: 'evidence PDF + JSON', kind: 'dep' },
];
---

<section id="architecture">
  <div class="wrap grid two">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
      <h2>Boring, well-understood parts</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        A FastAPI service and a Celery worker over PostgreSQL, Redis, OPA and any S3-compatible
        store. One <code>docker compose</code> file runs all of it. There is no proprietary runtime
        and nothing phones home.
      </p>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>Immutable classifications, policy checks and audit rows, enforced by database triggers</li>
        <li>Request IDs through API, logs, audit trail and worker tasks</li>
        <li>Prometheus metrics, liveness and readiness probes, structured JSON logs</li>
        <li>If OPA is unreachable, checks fall back to declarative rules and record which engine ran</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="stack" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: the Next.js console calls the FastAPI service, which uses Open Policy Agent, PostgreSQL, Redis and S3 storage; a Celery worker generates evidence.">
      {
        services.map((s) => (
          <div class={`box ${s.kind}`}>
            <strong>{s.name}</strong>
            <span>{s.detail}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .facts {
    padding-left: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .facts li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .stack {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
    align-content: center;
  }
  .box {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    background: var(--surface);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .box span {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .box.ui {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    border-style: dashed;
  }
  .box.core {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
</style>
